WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.440 --> 00:00:04.700
No matter how you look at it, it's gotta be
a major bummer to be unceremoniously cut from

00:00:04.700 --> 00:00:06.580
one of the biggest films of all time.

00:00:06.630 --> 00:00:10.960
Late last year, it was announced that 13 Reasons
Why​ star Katherine Langford had been cast

00:00:10.969 --> 00:00:15.269
in a small but important role in ​Avengers:
Endgame​, but the talented actress was nowhere

00:00:15.269 --> 00:00:17.080
to be found in the final cut of the film.

00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:19.240
"That is… shocking.

00:00:19.620 --> 00:00:20.580
I'm shocked."

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:23.380
And now we know all the reasons why.

00:00:23.380 --> 00:00:27.600
Warning: you're about to hear some major spoilers
for Avengers: Endgame… starting right this

00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:28.600
minute.

00:00:28.700 --> 00:00:32.540
If you've already seen the film, you know
all too well that Tony Stark makes the ultimate

00:00:32.540 --> 00:00:36.480
sacrifice while reducing Thanos and his minions
to so much dust in the wind.

00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:40.920
As heart-wrenching as the moment is, it's
also the perfect conclusion to Stark's character

00:00:40.920 --> 00:00:41.520
arc.

00:00:41.720 --> 00:00:46.220
During Endgame's five-year time jump, we learn
that he's retreated from the public eye and

00:00:46.220 --> 00:00:49.560
had a daughter named Morgan Stark with the
love of his life, Pepper Potts.

00:00:49.620 --> 00:00:54.680
Realizing that he has a responsibility both
to the universe and to his own beloved family,

00:00:54.680 --> 00:00:59.200
Stark heroically offers up his own life so
that the Mad Titan can be defeated once and

00:00:59.200 --> 00:00:59.780
for all.

00:00:59.860 --> 00:01:04.720
During a recent appearance on MTV's Happy
Sad Confused podcast, co-directors Joe and

00:01:04.720 --> 00:01:09.520
Anthony Russo revealed that Katherine Langford
had been cast as an older version of Morgan.

00:01:09.520 --> 00:01:13.460
She was supposed to appear to Stark in the
same netherworld where Thanos finds young

00:01:13.460 --> 00:01:15.520
Gamora in Avengers: Infinity War.

00:01:15.520 --> 00:01:18.000
Does this plot development sound confusing
to you?

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:22.520
If so, the directors wholeheartedly agree…
and that's why Langford's scene ultimately

00:01:22.520 --> 00:01:24.040
wound up on the cutting room floor.

00:01:24.200 --> 00:01:26.200
As co-director Joe Russo explained:

00:01:35.220 --> 00:01:39.840
Even though the audience got to see the emotional
bond between Stark and young Morgan, the directors

00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:43.780
realized that the sudden appearance of an
older version of Morgan wouldn't really register

00:01:43.780 --> 00:01:44.520
with audiences.

00:01:44.880 --> 00:01:46.720
Co-director Anthony Russo admitted:

00:01:50.140 --> 00:01:53.800
Even though Langford isn't featured in the
final cut of Avengers: Endgame, there may

00:01:53.810 --> 00:01:59.030
be a silver lining to the unfortunate situation:
Obviously, her acting chops impressed Marvel

00:01:59.030 --> 00:02:01.320
Studios enough for them to cast her in the
role.

00:02:01.320 --> 00:02:06.100
With that in mind, it's entirely possible
that Morgan Stark may return to the MCU in

00:02:06.100 --> 00:02:08.660
a future film… although nothing has been
announced yet.

00:02:08.660 --> 00:02:12.520
Since Endgame's release, a lot of people have
speculated that the film is setting up the

00:02:12.530 --> 00:02:16.379
appearance of the Young Avengers, a superhero
team that's been featured in the pages of

00:02:16.380 --> 00:02:18.500
Marvel Comics since 2005.

00:02:18.600 --> 00:02:22.900
While the MCU's version of the Young Avengers
would probably differ from the comics, we're

00:02:22.900 --> 00:02:26.820
sure a few key players would ultimately make
the leap from the page to the screen.

00:02:26.820 --> 00:02:30.080
Chief among these: Cassie Lang, the daughter
of Ant-Man.

00:02:31.640 --> 00:02:33.320
"Daddy!"

00:02:35.580 --> 00:02:38.700
In the comic books, she becomes the crime-fighter
known as Stature.

00:02:38.700 --> 00:02:42.849
And then there's Clint Barton's daughter Lila,
who some viewers think might eventually take

00:02:42.849 --> 00:02:43.840
over as Hawkeye.

00:02:43.840 --> 00:02:48.240
There's also Harley Keener, Stark's young
buddy from Iron Man 3, who popped up at Stark's

00:02:48.240 --> 00:02:49.880
funeral in Avengers: Endgame.

00:02:49.980 --> 00:02:54.140
If the Young Avengers are going to figure
prominently in Marvel's Phase 4, why not tap

00:02:54.150 --> 00:02:56.099
the daughter of Iron Man to lead them?

00:02:56.100 --> 00:02:59.400
Here's hoping Langford was cast in Endgame
with an eye towards the future.

00:02:59.580 --> 00:03:03.540
With any luck, the actress will receive a
consolation prize for her abandoned cameo,

00:03:03.550 --> 00:03:07.870
and score a major recurring role in history's
biggest-ever film franchise.

00:03:07.870 --> 00:03:12.140
Otherwise, yeah, that is a serious bummer…
for Langford, and for us.

